// Expected: c1u1 at one session and at two.
//
// Two shares of a 2-of-3 sharing travel in the clear, and secret itself is
// sent in the clear in phase 1. The attacker has recomposed secret from
// share_a and share_b at the phase-0 barrier; observing it on the wire in
// phase 1 is a disclosure independent of both shares, so the split ties the
// shares to it: u1. Knowledge used to keep only the first way it obtained a
// value, so a later disclosure left secret recorded as recomposed from the
// two queried shares, and withholding either one dropped it: u0 (GitHub issue
// #38, reported for a phase-1 leak).
attacker[passive]

principal Alice[
	generates secret
	share_a, share_b, share_c = THRESHOLD_SPLIT[2](secret)
]

Alice -> Bob: share_a, share_b

principal Bob[
	_ = HASH(share_a, share_b)
]

phase[1]

Alice -> Bob: secret

queries[
	confidentiality? secret
	unlinkability? share_a, share_b
]
